,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799200279,"data":"  The gate above ran on THIS card. Every timing number below is a timing of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799202731,"data":"  four expressions that were just shown to compute the same operator.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799205472,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799207827,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79921011,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799212569,"data":"3. the table: 64 slab(s) of [64,64], on the card\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799214973,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799217481,"data":"  MEASURED on this device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799219865,"data":"  launches  GlobalCounters.kernel_count -- kernels the device actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799222316,"data":"  kernel_us sum of the per-kernel CUDA-event times tinygrad PRINTS at DEBUG=2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799224755,"data":"            DEBUG=2 sets ExecContext.wait (realize.py:318), and ops_cuda.py:26-35\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799227296,"data":"            then records an event, launches, records a second event and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799229841,"data":"            SYNCHRONISES on it -- so the graph is serialised and each number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799232296,"data":"            contains that kernel's host launch latency. That is the instrument,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799237233,"data":"            not the card, and it is why the per-launch calibration in section 5\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799239875,"data":"            is needed to subtract it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799242263,"data":"  copy_us   time_sum_s minus kernel_us. exec_copy returns no elapsed time, so\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799244721,"data":"            realize.py:78-81 charges every COPY its HOST cost into time_sum_s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79924719,"data":"            It is a real cost and it is not device time.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799249623,"data":"  t_sched   HOST wall clock of Tensor.schedule_linear() on its own fresh graph.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799252099,"data":"  t_exec    HOST wall clock of Tensor.realize() + synchronize() on its own\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799254852,"data":"            fresh graph. Never on a graph already through schedule_linear():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799257387,"data":"            that MUTATES it (tensor.py:409-411) and the realize is then a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799259891,"data":"            silent no-op. How many kernels each timed realize launched is in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799262371,"data":"            ut_time.json, and a zero aborts the run.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799264808,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79926711,"data":"cand  launches  census_k  kernel_us   spread   copy_us  time_sum  ops(device)  t_sched_ms  t_exec_ms  t_build_ms  what\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799269679,"data":"----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
