,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799566393,"data":"C      5         566            5.1   0.7576      67.6%     0.077  floor 68% / arith 32%  launches flat: True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.7995689,"data":"D2     5         588           14.7   0.9862      39.0%     0.009  floor 39% / arith 61%  launches flat: True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799571415,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799573704,"data":"  `fixed` is the launch-dominated floor and `slope` the marginal per-slab\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799576158,"data":"  cost. `ns/MAC` is nanoseconds of device time per algorithmic multiply-add.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799578623,"data":"  If that number is roughly the same for two candidates, device time tracks\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799581089,"data":"  the ALGORITHM's arithmetic. If it differs by an order of magnitude between\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79958353,"data":"  them, device time is tracking the SCHEDULE and the arithmetic column is not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799586011,"data":"  what the card is spending its time on. `launches flat` is the precondition\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799588462,"data":"  for reading the fit this way at all, and it is reported per candidate.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799590906,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799593171,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799595644,"data":"5. launch calibration: what does one launch cost on this card?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799598063,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799600527,"data":"  A chain of n dependent one-op kernels, timed with the SAME instrument as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799602975,"data":"  the candidates (DEBUG=2, per-kernel CUDA events). The slope of kernel_us\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799605436,"data":"  against the number of kernels that ACTUALLY LAUNCHED is microseconds per\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799607919,"data":"  launch. This is the number that lets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799610331,"data":"      non_launch_us = kernel_us - launches * per_launch_us\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799612768,"data":"  be a residual in MICROSECONDS rather than an instruction count times a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799616158,"data":"  constant -- which is what the census's non-additivity demands.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799620253,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799622816,"data":"     shape      n  launched   kernel_us  us/launch\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799628497,"data":"--------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799631279,"data":"  1 thread     16        16         194     12.152\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799633761,"data":"  1 thread     64        64         750     11.717\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799636164,"data":"  1 thread    256       256       2,911     11.371\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799638888,"data":"  1 thread   1024     1,024      11,735     11.460\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79964134,"data":"  1 thread   4096     4,096      45,247     11.047\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799643829,"data":"  1 thread    fit                           11.033   intercept 128 us, R2 0.9999\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79964639,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799648672,"data":"     16 KB     16        16         195     12.176\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799651092,"data":"     16 KB     64        64         731     11.425\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799653485,"data":"     16 KB    256       256       2,975     11.620\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799655865,"data":"     16 KB   1024     1,024      11,700     11.426\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799658242,"data":"     16 KB   4096     4,096      46,954     11.463\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799660813,"data":"     16 KB    fit                           11.460   intercept 6 us, R2 1.0000\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799663359,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799665642,"data":"  MEASURED, DEBUG=2, so these slopes INCLUDE the host launch latency the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799668174,"data":"  instrument charges to every kernel -- which is exactly what the candidate\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799670738,"data":"  measurements are charged too, so the residual below compares like with like.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799673259,"data":"  The chain has ONE copy per realize, not one per step, so the intercept\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799675761,"data":"  absorbs the copy's host cost (realize.py:78-81) and the slope does not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799678263,"data":"  The `16 KB` row is a sensitivity check: it is what a candidate kernel of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799680716,"data":"  this operator's size costs if it did NOTHING but move one buffer. The\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799683168,"data":"  headline uses the `1 thread` row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799685548,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799687819,"data":"== residual: kernel_us - launches * per_launch_us   (bench shape) ==\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799690315,"data":"cand  launches  kernel_us  launch_us     @16KB   resid_us   resid %   ns/algMAC  reading\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799692792,"data":"----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79969535,"data":"A        5,380     91,175     59,358    61,655     31,816     34.9%       1.271  launch-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799697841,"data":"B           86      2,765        949       986      1,816     65.7%       0.073  not-launch-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799700338,"data":"C           44        840        485       504        355     42.2%       0.084  launch-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799702828,"data":"D2          41      1,483        452       470      1,031     69.5%       0.010  not-launch-dominated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79970773,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799710198,"data":"  `launches` here is the DEVICE launch count, which includes the COPYs. A COPY\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799712689,"data":"  costs no device time at all (exec_copy returns no elapsed time), so the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799715133,"data":"  launch term slightly over-charges every candidate. The number of COPYs is in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799717721,"data":"  ut_time.json per candidate; subtracting them changes the launch term by a few\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799721913,"data":"  percent and moves no row across the 50% line.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799724638,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.79972693,"data":"  ns/algMAC is nanoseconds of NON-LAUNCH device time per algorithmic\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799729942,"data":"  multiply-add, using the algorithm's own MAC count (ut_price.macs) and not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799732387,"data":"  any census figure. Candidates whose entries agree are being priced by the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799734912,"data":"  same axis; candidates whose entries differ by an order of magnitude are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799737376,"data":"  not, and THAT is the finding, not the winner.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799739757,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799742038,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799744499,"data":"7. is the ordering spelling-invariant?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799746878,"data":"==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799749323,"data":"  notes/31 §2: the `numpy` spelling of a constant costs a COPY kernel each and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799751884,"data":"  the `arange` spelling costs ALU inside every consumer. notes/31 measured the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799754362,"data":"  KERNEL ranking to be identical under both. The TIMING ranking is checked here,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799756829,"data":"  for the two candidates the open question is actually about.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1158.799759267,"data":"\n"}
